      "title": "Australia’s national medical research body advises conditional use of puberty blockers for transgender children",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/16/australias-national-medical-research-body-advises-conditional-use-of-puberty-blockers-for-transgender-children",
      "description": "<p>New National Health and Medical Research Council guidelines at odds with public hospital bans in Queensland and NT</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Australia’s largest medical research organisation has advised puberty blockers are appropriate for the gender-affirming care of young people in certain circumstances, after a year-long review of international evidence.</p><p>The federal government last year commissioned the commonwealth-funded National Health and Medical Research Council (NHMRC) to develop the advice in response to <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2025/jan/28/queensland-halts-prescription-of-puberty-blockers-and-hormones-for-children-with-gender-dysphoria\">bans in Queensland and Northern Territory</a> public hospitals imposed by their governments.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/16/australias-national-medical-research-body-advises-conditional-use-of-puberty-blockers-for-transgender-children\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-16T03:15:43"
    },
    {
      "title": "MP Helen Haines’ first words since leaving hospital after alleged attack led to double amputation",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/16/mp-helen-haines-out-of-hospital-after-attack-leg-amputation-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Independent MP says she is ‘overwhelmed’ by thousands of warm wishes and thanked Australians for charity donations</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The independent Australian MP Helen Haines has been discharged from hospital, four weeks after she was <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/24/helen-hainess-condition-improves-days-after-losing-both-legs-from-alleged-attack-ntwnfb\">allegedly attacked by a man</a> outside her electorate office in Victoria resulting in the double amputation of her legs.</p><p>In a statement, Haines said she had moved to the rehabilitation stage of her recovery, which would continue in Melbourne.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/16/mp-helen-haines-out-of-hospital-after-attack-leg-amputation-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-16T03:10:22"
    },
    {
      "title": "Senior Hells Angels bikie charged with threatening to kill investigative reporter Nick McKenzie",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/16/hells-angels-bikie-charged-threats-to-kill-journalist-nick-mckenzie-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Victoria police allege man, suspected of being a chapter president of the gang, sent ‘threats and harassing text messages’ to Nine journalist</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A senior Hells Angel has been charged with threatening to kill Nine’s investigative reporter Nick McKenzie, the Victorian police taskforce investigating corruption in the building sector has confirmed.</p><p>Police said detectives from the taskforce had charged a man on Monday, after he “sent a number of allegedly threatening, offensive and abusive text messages” to the Age journalist on Friday.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/16/hells-angels-bikie-charged-threats-to-kill-journalist-nick-mckenzie-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
