    {
      "title": "Coles investigates cyber-attack and apologises to customers",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/nov/16/coles-cyber-attack-incident-data",
      "description": "<p>Supermarket giant says no customer, team or supplier data compromised but recommends customers update passwords</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Australia’s second-largest retailer has been targeted in a cyber-attack, though it is still too early to tell whether any of its data has been stolen or compromised.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/coles\">Coles</a> revealed the threat on Monday morning, saying it was investigating with support from the Australian Cyber Security Centre and global security experts.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/nov/16/coles-cyber-attack-incident-data\">Continue reading...</a>",
